# Security Preflight buyer path candidate — 2026-08-06

## Decision

`SOURCE_CANDIDATE_READY / HOLD_PUBLICATION_AND_PRODUCTION`

The smallest evidence-backed commercial move is to turn the fresh Security
Preflight quote exposure into a complete buyer path. The live service already
returned one unpaid 402 to a distinct caller, but the official demo client did
not expose the route. That refusal may be an automated directory probe rather
than buyer intent. The public guides also advertised a Regulatory Radar watch
selector that the client did not implement.

This candidate closes both dead ends without moving money or weakening the
payment, security, or revenue claim boundaries.

## Candidate changes

- `scripts/x402_demo_client.py`
  - adds `--route security-preflight` with a complete, closed-schema safe
    example;
  - supports unpaid quote inspection with `--dry-run`;
  - retains the mandatory explicit ceiling for any single-route paid attempt;
  - adds the already-advertised `--route regulatory-watch` selector;
  - leaves the default five-route workflow unchanged.
- `deploy/gateway/quickstart.html`
  - adds a dedicated Security Preflight no-spend and one-attempt buyer path;
  - states the $1.00 list price, buyer-controlled ceiling, and live-quote
    authority;
  - states that the product performs static checks of caller-supplied artifacts
    and does not fetch or certify a runtime.
- `deploy/gateway/agents.html`
  - adds a direct Security Preflight quote-inspection call to action;
  - embeds the repaired cache-busted Gold402 badge;
  - preserves the adjacent disclosure that the directory verdict is not an
    endorsement, runtime audit, paid usage, or revenue;
  - reports the card's exact `Independent grade pending` boundary.
- four MCP publish manifests now match the already-running source versions:
  - Wavefunction Search `0.2.0` in both trees;
  - Subscriptions `0.1.1` in both trees.

## Live no-spend verification

The exact candidate client made unsigned POST requests to the two live routes.
Both returned HTTP 402; neither created a payment signature or attempted a
settlement.

Security Preflight:

- route: `/x402/security-preflight/security_preflight`;
- exact scheme on `eip155:8453`;
- official Base USDC asset:
  `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`;
- payee: `0xfEf2e570b645EB720Ee6c589d27450810982f329`;
- observed fresh quote: `10000` atomic USDC (`$0.01`);
- list price retained by the client: `1000000` atomic USDC (`$1.00`).

Regulatory Radar watch:

- route: `/x402/regulatory-radar/monitor_changes`;
- same exact scheme, network, asset, and payee;
- observed fresh quote: `10000` atomic USDC (`$0.01`);
- list price retained by the client: `250000` atomic USDC (`$0.25`).

An initial Security Preflight probe correctly failed with HTTP 400 because the
example included the gateway-owned internal `action`. The candidate removed
that field, and the repeated live no-spend probe passed. The regression test
now asserts that callers never send `action`.

## Verification

- focused activation and Hermes buyer tests: `29 passed`;
- broader x402, A2A, shared-contract, activation, and buyer tests:
  `127 passed`;
- full fleet after historical-control reconciliation:
  `2091 passed`, `0 failed`, `0 errors`, `36/36 clean`;
- local version coherence after manifest repair:
  `FLEET COHERENCE PASS — 27 agents, local`;
- clean public-main patch tests: `8 passed, 3 deselected`;
- public-main patch: local commit `ee2b479` on
  `codex/security-preflight-buyer-path-20260806`;
- public-main patch was prepared from clean remote commit `38de8e1` and was not
  pushed.

The five earlier full-suite failures had one pre-existing release-control root
cause. The historical Regulatory Radar promotion bundle pinned
`gateway_runtime_parity.py` at SHA-256 `7c907d...`; two later normalization
changes produced `6b43fa...`. The exact historical bytes were recovered from
the dated execution record, independently reproduced at `7c907d...`, and
archived under the 2026-07-26 release history. The original historical path is
again byte-identical, while the hardened 2026-08-04 helper remains distinct at
`6b43fa...`. No historical manifest, receipt, or pinned hash was rewritten.

This reconciliation cleared all 230 droplet tests, all 136 script tests, and
the complete 2,091-test fleet gate. A stale Glama assertion was also aligned to
the already-coherent Subscriptions `0.1.1` publish manifest.

